.TH GKBD 1 "2026-07-25" "gigactl 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gkbd \- control the keyboard backlight on Gigabyte G5/G6 laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gkbd
.I color
.br
.B gkbd
.I RRGGBB
.br
.B gkbd brightness
.I percent
.br
.B gkbd off
.br
.B gkbd on
.br
.B gkbd status
.br
.B gkbd apply
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gkbd
sets the colour and brightness of the single\-zone RGB keyboard backlight
through the Embedded Controller.
.PP
It works in one of two modes, chosen automatically each time it runs.
.TP
.B daemon
The
.BR gigactld (8)
service owns its D\-Bus name, so it is both the single writer of the Embedded
Controller and the owner of the saved backlight state, which it re\-applies at
boot and after suspend.
.B gkbd
becomes an unprivileged client of it: no
.BR sudo ,
no
.BR ec_probe ,
and \(em deliberately \(em no writes to
.BR gkbd 's
own store, because two stores for one backlight is how a stale colour wins a
race.
.TP
.B direct
No daemon is running, so
.B gkbd
drives the controller itself, keeps its own saved state in
.IR /var/lib/gkbd ,
and re\-runs itself under
.BR sudo (8).
Concurrent invocations serialise on
.IR /run/lock/gigactl\-ec.lock .
This mode needs the
.B ec_probe
utility from nbfc\-linux.
.PP
If neither can be established \(em no
.BR busctl (1)
on the system, or the bus does not answer \(em
.B gkbd
refuses to do anything rather than risk writing the controller behind a running
daemon's back.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I color
One of
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR blue ,
.BR white ,
.BR orange ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR purple
(or
.BR violet )
and
.BR pink .
.TP
.I RRGGBB
An explicit colour in hexadecimal, with or without a leading
.BR # ,
for example
.B ff6600
or
.BR '#00ff88' .
.TP
.B brightness \fIpercent\fR
Set backlight brightness, 0 to 100.
.TP
.B off
Switch the backlight off.
.TP
.B on
Switch the backlight on, restoring the last colour and brightness.
.TP
.B status
Print the current colour and brightness. In daemon mode this is what the daemon
holds; in direct mode it is what
.B gkbd
last saved.
.TP
.B apply
Re\-apply the saved state. This exists for the standalone restore service that
predates the daemon; when the daemon is running it owns restore, so this reports
that there is nothing to do rather than writing an older value over a newer one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B gkbd
exits 0 on success and 1 on failure: an unsupported machine, an unrecognised
colour, a lock held by another writer, or a daemon whose presence could not be
determined.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GKBD_UNSAFE
Set to
.B 1
to skip the vendor and model check. The Embedded Controller protocol was
reverse engineered on a Gigabyte G6 KF; on hardware from another ODM the same
registers can mean anything at all, so overriding this risks the machine.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/gkbd/state
Colour and brightness saved by direct mode. Not used, and not written, while the
daemon is running \(em it keeps its own state in
.IR /var/lib/gigactl/state.json .
.TP
.I /run/lock/gigactl\-ec.lock
Serialises Embedded Controller access between
.BR gkbd ,
.BR gfan (1)
and
.BR gigactld (8).
.SH NOTES
Verified on the Gigabyte G6 KF. Other G5, G6 and G7 models are expected to
work \(em they are the same Clevo\-ODM platform \(em and print a notice saying
they are untested. Anything else is refused.
.PP
The backlight is a single zone: one colour for the whole keyboard. The
controller wants its colour bytes in blue, red, green order and ignores every
lighting command until it has been sent a master enable, both of which are
handled here and documented with the protocol.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gfan (1),
.BR gigactl-gui (1),
.BR gigactld (8)
.PP
The reverse\-engineered controller protocol is documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/gigactl
and at
.UR https://github.com/smairio/gigactl
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
khalil Smairi
